    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>Is the Keychron Q1 better than the Keychron K8?</h3>
    <p>The Keychron Q1 is better for enthusiasts who want a premium CNC aluminum body, gasket-mounted typing feel, hot-swap switches, and QMK/VIA customization. The Keychron K8 is better for budget buyers and Mac users who want a wireless, tenkeyless keyboard with a simple, reliable experience for around $50 less.</p>

    <h3>Which Keychron keyboard is better for typing, the K8 or the Q1?</h3>
    <p>The Keychron Q1 delivers a superior typing feel thanks to its gasket-mounted plate, sound-dampening foam, and heavier aluminum case that absorb vibration and produce a deeper, more cushioned sound. The K8 types well for its price but has a firmer, more hollow sound typical of plastic tray-mount boards.</p>

    <h3>Is the Keychron K8 or Q1 better for Mac users?</h3>
    <p>Both work well on Mac, but the Keychron K8 is the more convenient choice for most Mac users because it is wireless with Bluetooth multipoint and includes a Mac-specific keycap layout out of the box. The Q1 is also Mac-compatible and includes Mac keycaps, but its wired-only design suits users who want a permanent desk keyboard.</p>

    <h3>Can I swap switches on the Keychron K8 and Keychron Q1?</h3>
    <p>Both keyboards support hot-swap, but with different scope. The Keychron Q1 includes hot-swap sockets as standard on every variant, letting you change switches without soldering. The Keychron K8 offers a hot-swap variant that must be selected at purchase; the standard K8 has soldered switches and cannot be swapped without desoldering.</p>

    <h3>Does the Keychron Q1 support QMK and VIA?</h3>
    <p>Yes, the Keychron Q1 supports full QMK and VIA programmability, letting you remap every key, build custom layers, configure macros, and tweak RGB lighting through a visual interface. The Keychron K8 does not support QMK or VIA and offers only limited remapping through Keychron's software, making the Q1 the clear choice for users who want deep customization.</p>

    <h3>Which Keychron keyboard is better for gaming?</h3>
    <p>The Keychron Q1 is better for gaming thanks to its wired-only connection, which eliminates Bluetooth latency and provides the lowest possible input lag. Its gasket-mounted plate also produces a more satisfying tactile feedback for fast key presses. The Keychron K8 is adequate for casual gaming over Bluetooth, but competitive gamers who need every millisecond of responsiveness should choose the Q1's wired connection.</p>

